# mod_GLQS
!! The cheatsp entry in cheatVars gates whether the Quick Setup link shows up
!! at all, and previously had no default - QSP vars start at 0 (falsy) until
!! explicitly set, so every new save silently hid the link until a player
!! happened to find the Enabled/Disabled toggle - which until now lived in a
!! route nothing ever called, so in practice there was no way to reach it.
!! Default it on the first time it is ever seen (tracked by a companion flag,
!! since 0 alone cannot distinguish never-set from explicitly-disabled), so the
!! link works out of the box. The switch to hide it later is on the GLQS Index.
if cheatVars['cheatsp_defaulted'] <> 1:
	cheatVars['cheatsp'] = 1
	cheatVars['cheatsp_defaulted'] = 1
end

!! mod_GLQS is auto-invoked by the games own mod loader (core_loop in
!! mod_system.qsrc, wired up via $onnewloc = LOCA in start.qsrc) after
!! EVERY real gt transition anywhere in the game, but the link itself is
!! meant to only show inside the players own room - three specific
!! screens: the current home bedroom, the uni dorm room, and the
!! therapist hotel room (a temp-lodging screen visited during that
!! questline). This was the mods original pre-0.29.12 scope; it was
!! briefly widened to every real location and then narrowed back here
!! since a MOD link cluttering ordinary gameplay screens (shops, NPC
!! homes, city locations) was worse than the convenience of it following
!! the player everywhere. func(''homes_properties'', ''is_current_home'',
!! $curloc) plus $locclass = ''bedr'' catches the bedroom of whichever
!! property is the players current home (owned, rented, or family) -
!! $locclass is set per-location by the game itself, not derived here.
!! The dorm and therapist checks match $loc/$curloc/$loc_arg exactly as
!! the game sets them for those two specific rooms.
!! Two extra guards on top of the room check: opPRE > 0 marks character
!! creation still in progress (set in start.qsrc at the very first screen,
!! cleared at the end of intro_initialization.qsrc) - mc stats do not
!! fully exist yet, so cheats would error or behave strangely if triggered
!! there. location_type = event marks the games own scripted scenes (sex
!! scenes, big story beats) which can happen inside the bedroom itself
!! and should not be interrupted with an unrelated UI link.
!! Every entry link calls enter (04_main_menu.qsps) with the screen to go
!! back to. From a room that is $loc, $loc_arg - the games own idiom for the
!! screen the player is on (the act Continue: gt $loc, $loc_arg pattern in
!! core_library.qsrc).
if opPRE = 0 and $location_type <> 'event' and cheatVars['cheatsp'] = 1 and ((func('homes_properties', 'is_current_home', $curloc) and $locclass = 'bedr') or ($loc = 'uni_dorm' and $curloc = 'uni_dorm' and $loc_arg = 'dorm_room') or ($loc = 'HotelRoom' and $curloc = 'HotelRoom' and $loc_arg = 'therapist')):
	'<b> MOD <a href="exec: gs ''mod_GLQS_main'', ''enter'', $loc, $loc_arg & gt ''mod_GLQS_main'', ''start''">Quick Setup</a> MOD</b>'
end

!! Also offered under every tab of the games own cheat menu, which is reachable
!! from anywhere. Every tab is a real gt into cheatmenu_din, and the hook gets
!! the gt arguments, so ARGS[0] is the open tab and Return can come back to it.
!! Not gated on the room-link toggle - that switch is about keeping ordinary
!! gameplay screens clean, and the cheat menu is already a cheat screen.
if opPRE = 0 and $curloc = 'cheatmenu_din':
	'<br><b> MOD <a href="exec: gs ''mod_GLQS_main'', ''enter'', ''cheatmenu_din'', ''' + $ARGS[0] + ''' & gt ''mod_GLQS_main'', ''start''">Open GLQS</a> MOD</b>'
end

--- mod_GLQS ---------------------------------

# mod_GLQS_options
!! Reached from Settings > Mods, where the base game renders a link labelled
!! $mod_info[4] for any mod that sets it ($mod_opt in mod_system.qsrc, linked
!! from display_mod_table in _menu_settings.qsrc). It opens the GLQS menu
!! directly; the room-link switch that used to live here is on the GLQS Index.
gs 'mod_GLQS_main', 'enter', '$menu_settings', 'mods'
gt 'mod_GLQS_main', 'start'
--- mod_GLQS_options ---------------------------------
